 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122828 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122828 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122828 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122828 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f3f8e063-53b4-59b1-a70a-2cbd7cdb3bd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186122841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122840 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "086dfdbb-92b2-5cae-9238-3f1a3c6feab0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122841 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{r}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122841 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122841 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a6f0a484-c1df-59cd-8a67-536b8a6b6fae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122842 #edb/ref 1080 "r" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d6d87c61-ce4c-51b4-a48d-e8a1bd1e34a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124082 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0b6129c-b733-5c71-92b5-462c14e827e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124405 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124405 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\dfrac12x^2+y^2,$ find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial \\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124405 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4940fa22-1584-565f-81fe-dc12e5132f23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124405 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂f}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂f}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta } & =-(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124406 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8295" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124406 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $w(r, \\theta)=r \\cos 3\\theta,$ find $\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124406 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a0246ee6-702f-5d8d-8482-8db1c46b32ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124406 #edb/ref 1074 "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} = \\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial r}\\cos\\theta - \\dfrac{1}{r}\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial \\theta}\\sin\\theta\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }=-3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(-3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124407 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124407 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $w(x,y,z)=z^3(x^2+2y^2),$ find $\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial \\theta},$ where $(x,y,z)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta,z)$ are the corresponding cylindrical polar coordinates." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124407 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c1e69bbe-b079-56e5-9ce0-296785d73100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124407 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $w(x,y,z)$ with three independent variables $r, \\theta,$ and $z,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta, y=r\\sin\\theta,$ and $z=z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂w}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂w}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $x$ and $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x}=2x{z}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=4y{z}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r, \\theta,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =2r{z}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =4r{z}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta } & =-(2r{z}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(4r{z}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-2{r}^{2}{z}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{r}^{2}{z}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}{z}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}{z}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124594 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175